# meta-deploy.list: the queue meta-deploy.bash runs, in this order.
#
# STANDING RULE (CLAUDE/AgentNotes.md): this list is exactly what needs running NOW. Add a
# run when it is pending, remove it once it has run and is done, leave out what cannot
# usefully run yet, then ask the owner to run meta-deploy.bash. Every step a run needs lives
# in the plan's own scripts, so this is the only command the owner is handed. The order is by
# dependency. A plan with none of triage.bash, deploy.bash and acceptance.bash has nothing
# for the script to do. A triage-only plan is run once, read-only. Words after the folder
# name are passed to that plan's triage.bash, both runs.
#
# One entry per line, four kinds:
#   <plan folder>                  its triage, deploy and acceptance scripts, in order
#   playbooks/<path>.yml           a change no plan owns; run as one unit through its own
#                                  shebang, which goes through run.bash, exactly as
#                                  ./playbooks/imports/<play>.yml does by hand
#   <plan folder>/<script>.bash    one plan script, for a step none of the three fixed names
#                                  fits; run as one unit, like a playbook entry, except
#                                  that a script named *acceptance*.bash may exit 2 for
#                                  COULD NOT ESTABLISH, as an acceptance.bash may
#   changed-plays                  every play that has run here and has to run again, as
#                                  one unit: the checkout's ./run.bash --changed --yes, in
#                                  playbook-main.yml order, stopping at the first failure
#
# changed-plays runs WHERE IT STANDS in the list, like every other entry, and decides which
# plays it runs when it starts, so the entries above it have already run (a play an entry
# above ran is no longer changed, and is not run twice). Put it above the plan entries whose
# deploy or acceptance expects the changed plays to have run, which is the usual case, and
# below an entry it must follow. It replaces a hand-copied list of stale plays: name a
# playbooks/ entry only for a play that must run at a fixed point between two plan steps.
# Its description says which changed plays the agent expects it to pick up and why.
#
# A line starting with # is a comment and is the description of the entry below it: it is how
# the owner learns what a run will do, so write it. Blank lines are ignored. Any other line
# that is not an entry is a fatal error naming its line number.
# Plan 00185 Task 1.1 (#60, wrong emoji glyphs): TRIAGE ONLY, READ-ONLY. The plan has only
# triage.bash; it changes nothing on the host, needs no sudo and never prompts. It records the
# terminal it runs in and every running terminal emulator (version, start time), the VTE
# version, the emoji font packages and their install times, fc-match and fc-list for the
# issue's code points, the fontconfig cache ages, which emoji font file each running terminal
# has mapped, and the terminals' font and GPU settings. Start meta-deploy from the terminal that
# draws the wrong emoji, and leave that window open while it runs.
00185-terminal-emoji-glyphs
# Plan 00213 Tasks 1.3, 1.4 and 2.3 (the bus status line in Go): deploy.bash runs the whole
# play-agent-bus.yml again (it passed on its own at 67033c224, so no change), then the whole
# play-claude-yolo.yml, then acceptance.bash. The kit's settings.json runs the static Go
# pingbus-status-line, copied into every running LXC member. The ccy play gives the host CCY
# 3.100.8 (the Go front, the image build lock and --opencode: see the play-claude-yolo.yml entry
# below) and puts the binary in the image's build context. That play run builds the image,
# container 2.79.3: it downloads opencode 1.19.3 from github.com and stops this entry if its
# sha256 is not the pinned one, so an opencode download failure shows here (the image
# also carries the farewell-reason fix, the reports and questions admin tool and Go 1.26.10 in the project image): a seated session's status line is
# the Go one and refreshes every 25 s. The acceptance checks the kit's, the image's and each
# online declared LXC member's binary are this checkout's build (a member whose container is
# stopped is named offline and not judged, never a failure), runs the recorded Python goldens against the installed Python and Go, and
# measures the CPU one render costs in each: Go must cost under a fifth (the report has the
# figures). Needs sudo once. Afterwards restart the teams' agent sessions; a running one keeps
# its old status line.
00213-agent-bus-performance-go-carve-out/deploy.bash
# Plan 00211 deploy 2 (Task 2.6), the reports and questions rooms, LAST. It needs every team's
# agent sessions restarted since pingbus 0.2.0 was installed, ccy and LXC alike, which the
# host reboot did. A team member that is offline (its container stopped, or its session not
# running) is named as offline and never blocks the run. This runs
# deploy.bash --stage 2: it refuses unless the spike report says every fact holds, then runs
# acceptance.bash --stage 1 again as the pre-flight (the host's and every online declared LXC
# member's pingbus is 0.2.0; an offline member is named, not judged). Then the
# whole play-agent-bus.yml keeps each team's reports and questions rooms (created when
# play-agent-bus.yml passed at 67033c224), the index and the invites; the whole play-claude-yolo.yml finds the ccy image already
# at container 2.79.3. Then acceptance.bash --stage 2 waits up to 180 s for every online
# coordinator to join its questions room and every running ccy seat its reports room, naming
# any that has not (an offline coordinator is named, not waited for), and checks the rooms
# (agent-bus check-rooms prints a coordinator with no live status as OFFLINE and passes; one
# whose session is listening but has not joined is a problem). It
# finds the first team's coordinator in its running ccy session or LXC member; with no team
# coordinator it is REJECTED, named, before it changes anything. It adds and removes one
# throwaway worker that must be refused the questions room and whose test report must reach no
# online inbox, posts a second test report from inside an online LXC member (with none, that
# check is NOT JUDGED), and has the coordinator ask a test question (NOT JUDGED when the
# coordinator is offline). Needs sudo once. Afterwards, if the test question was asked, do the
# Element steps of the plan's ACCEPTANCE-owner.md.
00211-agent-bus-reports-and-questions-rooms/deploy-stage-2.bash
# Plan 00201 Task 2.7 (M7): the automated two-team acceptance again, because its M3 check
# (the session's status line) changed since it last passed, and Plan 00213's cut-over made
# that status line the Go one. acceptance.bash only: it makes two throwaway teams declared
# in a run-directory host_vars (your host_vars and teams are never touched), runs one headless
# ccy session on both and a plain one (each one short turn on haiku), checks descriptions,
# launch block, per-session record, status line, `say` and SessionEnd, then purges both teams
# and checks their firewalld rules are gone, however the run ends. Needs sudo once, ccy
# launched interactively in this checkout once (Quick Launch), and the hooks daemon installed.
00201-ccy-teams-many-teams-per-session-descriptions-and-a-picker
# play-claude-yolo.yml, the whole play (Plan 00191 Tasks 4.3, 4.4, 4.4b and 4.5, Plans 00216,
# 00201 and 00215): the host's ccy becomes CCY 3.100.8. Plan 00216: only one image build runs at a time; two
# ccy launches started together build the image once, the second waiting (it says on stderr every
# 30 s whose build it waits for) and then using that build. The play's own image build takes the
# same lock (lib/image-build-lock.bash, newly installed with lib/image-build.bash), so it waits
# for a launch's build and a launch waits for it. `ccy --build-lock` (answered by the Go front)
# shows the build in progress and stops a hung one after a [y/N]. Check after the run: start
# `ccy --rebuild=full` in two terminals at the same moment: the second prints the waiting line
# and starts its own build only when the first has finished (an explicit rebuild always builds);
# while one builds, `ccy --build-lock` in a third terminal names it, and `n` leaves it running.
# The play builds the image every run, so it is already container 2.79.3 here (its guide, the
# room-ID fix in its pingbus, Plan 00211, Plan 00201's declare.py, agent-bus check-rooms passing an offline
# coordinator, Plan 00211, and opencode 1.19.3, the open-source coding agent,
# checked against its pinned sha256 at build), built by the 00213 entry above; the next launch
# rebuilds only a project's own image. Plan 00215: new flag `ccy --opencode` (or -oc) runs
# opencode in the container instead of Claude Code, with no bus kit and no supervisor; it needs a
# model provider key file first, in ~/.claude-tokens/ccy/provider-keys/, which the play makes
# empty (docs/ccy.md, "opencode"; Plan 00215 Task 1.4), and without one it
# stops before anything starts; an opencode session is not restored after a reboot, and a Quick
# Launch's saved team is not taken by it (or by --no-bus), and is kept for the next launch. A
# launch without the flag is unchanged.
# Plan 00201: the play rebuilds ~/.local/bin/ccy-teams with the lxc-add fix: `ccy-teams lxc-add
# <team>` for a member the host_vars already declare says "<user>@<container> is already declared in team <team>"
# and, after one yes, applies the team (play-agent-bus.yml) without writing; declared otherwise,
# it names each differing key and offers to update the entry or stop. A refusal of the
# host_vars file stops at once, naming the file, instead of asking the same question three
# times; `ccy-teams create` stops the same way, and a gh lookup that fails for any reason but
# GitHub's 404 (no network, a login gone stale) ends it with gh's words instead of asking for
# another name; the settings screen stops, instead of asking again, on a team the host_vars no
# longer declare. Check: run `ccy-teams lxc-add <team>` for the member that was refused before.
# /var/local/claude-yolo/claude-yolo becomes a Go program (built here from
# src-go/cmd/claude-yolo, installed only when its checksum changes) that answers --version,
# --help, --list-tokens, --token-usage [--json], --prevent and --export-token NAME itself
# (everything else, --top and the interactive export included, stays in the bash) and execs
# the bash launcher, now installed beside it as claude-yolo.bash, for every other run with the
# same arguments and environment plus CCY_LAUNCHER_FRONT, its own path, which the bash takes
# (only if it is the claude-yolo beside it) and unsets so its sessions re-run the Go program. If it
# misbehaves, CCY_LEGACY=1 ccy ... runs the bash launcher for everything; if it will not start,
# /var/local/claude-yolo/claude-yolo.bash run directly keeps the whole session on the bash;
# to go back entirely, run this play from the revision
# before Task 4.5 (it copies the bash over claude-yolo again, and leaves this claude-yolo.bash
# behind, stale but harmless: session records and re-runs name claude-yolo, and the plan
# scripts that read the launcher as text read claude-yolo whenever it is a script, so nothing
# runs or reads it; a session recorded by 3.99.14.0 before this fix would run it, and so would
# a session started by running claude-yolo.bash directly, which records that file: after a
# rollback, restoring such a session runs the stale .bash copy). Check after
# the run:
# `ccy --version`, `ccy --help`, `ccy --list-tokens`, `ccy --token-usage`, `ccy --prevent`
# and `ccy --export-token NAME` print the same bytes as `CCY_LEGACY=1 ccy ...` with the same
# flag (run --prevent and --export-token with a throwaway token name: they change state).
# lib/tmux-session.bash no longer carries the unused bash take-over
# (taking a session over stays the ccy-sessions picker's Ctrl-T); the new lib/host-paths.bash
# lets the launcher's differential harness point the build context, GPU directory and zone
# database elsewhere (unset, nothing changes) and refuses a bad or relative override at
# start; the launcher's temporary files follow TMPDIR when it is set; the GitHub and Claude
# tokens are no longer exported to every program the launcher starts, only handed by name to
# the container runs that need them; a GH_TOKEN you export reaches the session through the new
# lib/token-handoff.bash (a private file whose path only goes to the tmux re-run, deleted at
# once; any other path in CCY_GH_TOKEN_HANDOFF is refused); --debug's log is 0600 with tokens
# of a known prefix masked (the terminal still shows the raw trace). Container 2.79.3 (the guide in the image is corrected,
# its pingbus has the room-ID fix, Plan 00201's declare.py is in it, its agent-bus check-rooms passes an offline coordinator, and opencode is added), built by the play itself. It also rebuilds ~/.local/bin/ccy-teams with
# Plan 00209 stage 1 (the team, seat and declare reads in-process), which the check below
# judges. Afterwards start a ccy session as usual: it
# must rebuild, start and attach as before, and gh must work inside it.
playbooks/imports/play-claude-yolo.yml
# Plan 00209 stage 1 host check, after the play-claude-yolo.yml entry above has installed the
# ccy-teams that reads team, seat and declare state in-process. READ-ONLY: it changes nothing,
# and keeps two builds and every output in its run directory. It checks the installed ccy-teams
# is this checkout's build, builds the ccy-teams from before stage 1 from git, and runs each three
# times in turn: `--list` must print the same bytes (a difference in every round rejects, one in
# some rounds only is a live change and a note) and run faster (it took 9-23 s before), and an
# open, drawn on this terminal from an empty folder under TMPDIR that is in no checkout and
# answered with Esc at its first screen, must be faster and start exactly one declare status and
# no agent-bus seat list. A member.json that sets report_per_hour must be listed, not refused:
# on a fixture in the run directory (always, and the report says so) and on any live seat. Needs
# sudo once (so both read the member rosters) and a terminal. A failure names the check, and a
# --list diff is in the report. An open whose first screen is a question leaves S3 NOT JUDGED
# (exit 2, COULD NOT ESTABLISH in the summary), and the run log names the question. It comes
# back on every open: for a team limited to some folders or with no description, until that is
# settled or never chosen; while teams are out of date, until they are applied; with no team,
# until one is made. Settle it in ccy-teams and run again.
00209-agent-bus-v2-in-go/acceptance-s1.bash
# Plan 00214 acceptance (issue #110), LAST, with no changed-plays entry above it: it needs plays
# still to run. Runs no play and needs no sudo. It checks that the health report's
# play-freshness check and run.bash --changed's helper name the same plays (the report said 10
